<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>2.14.3: Self Check</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00632</md:content-id>
    <md:title>2.14.3: Self Check</md:title>
    <md:uuid>e3436479-6a2a-46ac-9a39-ebe3e999332f</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para dir="ltr"> </para>
<para dir="ltr"><span id="docs-internal-guid-eba221b0-7fff-0811-4aab-876d1094b1c9">A music store is shipping guitars and snare drums. </span></para><span id="docs-internal-guid-eba221b0-7fff-0811-4aab-876d1094b1c9">
  <list>
    <item><span id="docs-internal-guid-eba221b0-7fff-0811-4aab-876d1094b1c9"><span>Each guitar weighs 6 pounds.</span></span></item>
    <item><span id="docs-internal-guid-eba221b0-7fff-0811-4aab-876d1094b1c9"><span>Each snare drum weighs 14 pounds. </span></span></item>
    <item><span id="docs-internal-guid-eba221b0-7fff-0811-4aab-876d1094b1c9"><span>The maximum weight of guitars and snare drums cannot be more than 120 pounds.</span></span></item>
    <item><span id="docs-internal-guid-eba221b0-7fff-0811-4aab-876d1094b1c9"><span>The store needs to ship more than 10 total instruments.</span></span></item>
  </list>
  <para dir="ltr">Which of the following systems of inequalities describes the situation if \(x\) is the number of guitars and \(y\) is the number of snare drums?</para>
</span></section>
</content>
</document>
